    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0142" n="1102" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1102"/>

                <head>No. 760.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Gonnery.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 18,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 243.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit a copy of a letter from Messrs.
                    Alexandre &amp; Sons, dated the 12th instant, wherein they refer to the
                    introduction in the Mexican Congress of a bill, which, however, failed of
                    passage, granting to American steamers the 2 per cent. rebate in duties enjoyed
                    by the Spanish line of steamers.</p>
                <p>As the Department has no information upon this subject, I will thank you to
                    report whether such a bill was so introduced; and, if so, to obtain, if
                    possible, a copy thereof for the Department’s information, accompanied by a
                    translation of the same.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d47-a1.xml" xpointer="d47-a1"/>
            </div>
